# Everything here runs in Linux containers: LF on every platform, whatever
# core.autocrlf says (a Windows clone otherwise breaks every shebang).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Stacked pull requests each add lines at the same spot of the backlog and the
# ledger. The ledger is append-only: the union driver keeps both sides' added
# lines in a local merge or rebase instead of stopping on a conflict (GitHub's
# own merge ignores it). The backlog uses the devhost-todo driver
# (.github/scripts/merge_todo.py): union, then one line per backlog id, the
# ticked one preferred, so a tick both sides made no longer survives twice.
# `task repo:setup` registers the driver (.gitconfig). In a clone without it git
# falls back to its default merge (a conflict to resolve by hand), and the
# devhost-verify backlog_ids guard still refuses a repeated id.
TODO.md merge=devhost-todo
docs/ledger/*.md merge=union
